  {
    "title": "Security Operations - Network Intrusion Analysis and Detection for DevonCinema",
    "thumbnail": "https://files.elfsightcdn.com/eafe4a4d-3436-495d-b748-5bdce62d911d/1ec17497-f1b1-41ee-9e6e-8ff4c450babf/Screenshot-2025-01-10-at-15-08-18.png",
    "description": "Overview: This project analyzed a simulated cybersecurity incident targeting the DevonCinema network infrastructure. Using Wireshark and Snort, the investigation uncovered malicious activities, including unauthorized HTTP downloads, encrypted Command-and-Control (C2) communication, and lateral movement attempts. The findings were documented and formed the basis for a comprehensive long-term detection and response plan.",
    "long_description": "Overview: This project analyzed a simulated cybersecurity incident targeting the DevonCinema network infrastructure. Using Wireshark and Snort, the investigation uncovered malicious activities, including unauthorized HTTP downloads, encrypted Command-and-Control (C2) communication, and lateral movement attempts. The findings were documented and formed the basis for a comprehensive long-term detection and response plan.\n\nKey Achievements:\n\n1. Network Traffic Analysis:\n\n- Inspected `.pcap` files using Wireshark to identify infection vectors, suspicious downloads, and IoCs.\n\n- Applied filters for HTTP, SSL, SMB, and RPC traffic to uncover malicious communication patterns.\n\n2. Snort Configuration and Intrusion Detection:\n\n- Created custom Snort rules to detect malicious HTTP and ICMP traffic.\n\n- Analyzed `.pcap` files with Snort to correlate findings with predefined IoCs.\n\n- Confirmed malicious activity, including a RAT (Remcos) connecting to a C2 server.\n\n3. Incident Reporting and Recommendations:\n\n- Identified the infected system (`10.0.90.215`) and proposed mitigations for vulnerabilities.\n\n- Recommended deployment of IDS/IPS systems, SIEM solutions, and improved user training.\n\n- Outlined strategic long-term measures to prevent future incidents, focusing on proactive defense.\n\nSkills and Technologies:\n\n- Tools Used: Wireshark, Snort, VirusTotal.\n\n- Key Skills: Packet analysis, intrusion detection rule creation, network forensics, and vulnerability mitigation.\n\n- Methodology: Applied NIST guidelines for incident handling and leveraged open-source tools for forensic analysis.\n\nOutcome:\n\nThe project demonstrated expertise in network traffic analysis and the practical use of IDS/IPS systems. It provided actionable insights for improving cybersecurity defenses while showcasing a multi-layered approach to incident response.",
    "skills": [
      "NETWORK SECURITY",
      "WIRESHARK",
      "SNORT"
    ],
    "link": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MTIOb-VboC4ix-D8asxCPMVTNjqlUy95/view?usp=share_link",
    "categories": [
      "Defensive - Blue Teaming"
    ],
    "date": "2025-01-23",
    "images": [
      "https://files.elfsightcdn.com/eafe4a4d-3436-495d-b748-5bdce62d911d/85293ce2-e3ac-46cf-be46-4eaa79b693d0/SOIM.png"
    ],
    "id": "0f648b6d-575a-4bf1-a17b-658969026e51"
