  {
    "title": "Comprehensive Digital Forensics Report for Cybersecurity Incident Response",
    "thumbnail": "https://files.elfsightcdn.com/eafe4a4d-3436-495d-b748-5bdce62d911d/161d2243-5c9e-47be-80ee-82561090565f/Screenshot-2024-12-12-at-21-45-05.png",
    "description": "Conducted a digital forensic investigation to uncover unauthorized access to sensitive data. Activities included acquiring and analyzing digital evidence, investigating malicious activities, and delivering a detailed forensic report. Tools used include FTK Imager, Wireshark, Volatility, and Autopsy. Delivered actionable recommendations to strengthen cybersecurity practices and prevent future breaches.",
    "long_description": "Conducted a digital forensic investigation to uncover unauthorized access to sensitive data. Activities included acquiring and analyzing digital evidence, investigating malicious activities, and delivering a detailed forensic report. Tools used include FTK Imager, Wireshark, Volatility, and Autopsy. Delivered actionable recommendations to strengthen cybersecurity practices and prevent future breaches.\n\nThis project was part of a coursework requirement for the PUSL3133 module on Digital Forensics & Malware Analysis. The investigation revolved around an unauthorized data transfer incident at ABC Company. A digital forensic approach was applied to uncover the details of the breach, determine its scope, and recommend mitigation strategies.\n\nKey Objectives:\nQuantify the Data Loss: Identify the type and volume of data compromised to evaluate organizational risks.\nPreserve Digital Evidence: Collect and maintain evidence to ensure its admissibility in legal or organizational proceedings.\nIdentify the Culprit: Pinpoint whether the breach was internal or external, using activity logs, email analysis, and network traffic monitoring.\nEnhance Security Measures: Suggest immediate and long-term solutions to improve ABC Company’s cybersecurity posture.\nKey Steps and Techniques:\nDigital Evidence Acquisition:\nUtilized forensic tools such as FTK Imager to create bit-by-bit forensic images.\nMaintained the chain of custody by documenting hash values, timestamps, and tools used.\nAnalyzed stored email data, suspect files, and network logs.\nEmail Analysis:\nUsed tools like Autopsy, Kernel PST Viewer, and MXToolbox to investigate suspicious emails.\nConducted header analysis to detect spoofing attempts and email authentication failures (SPF, DKIM, DMARC).\nIdentified hidden data using steganography detection in attachments.\nNetwork Analysis:\nExamined anomalies in email headers and correlated them with network activity using MXToolbox.\nIdentified unauthorized access from suspicious IPs.\nJustification of Tools:\nEach tool was selected based on its ability to handle email metadata analysis, network traffic correlation, and forensic imaging.\nFindings and Recommendations:\nDiscovered spoofed email activity leading to data exfiltration.\nIdentified gaps in ABC Company’s email authentication protocols.\nRecommended implementing SPF, DKIM, and DMARC standards, advanced network monitoring, and employee training to mitigate future risks.\nChallenges Overcome:\nWorked with limited network traffic data (PCAP files were unavailable).\nEnsured data integrity and legal compliance while preserving the chain of custody.\nCoordinated analysis across various forensic tools to achieve comprehensive results.\nOutcome: The project successfully uncovered the details of the unauthorized data transfer, identified potential risks, and provided a roadmap for improving ABC Company’s cybersecurity defenses. This practical experience reinforced skills in email forensics, network analysis, and evidence handling while adhering to legal and organizational standards.\n\nThis project showcases my ability to apply theoretical knowledge in a real-world forensic investigation, demonstrating skills in teamwork, problem-solving, and advanced cybersecurity practices.",
    "skills": [
      "DIGITAL FORENSICS",
      "INCIDENT RESPONSE",
      "INVESTIGATION"
    ],
    "link": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1s8JWNwQjh_jxCIxMu2s3t1l9ufVEIJWq/view?usp=share_link",
    "categories": [
      "Defensive - Blue Teaming"
    ],
    "date": "2024-09-23",
    "images": [
