  {
    "title": "Azure Sentinel (SIEM) Lab",
    "thumbnail": "https://files.elfsightcdn.com/eafe4a4d-3436-495d-b748-5bdce62d911d/1bc4c394-d9ae-40e6-81bd-d9f1f7a80543/incident-severity.png",
    "description": "Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) - Sentinel-Lab. This innovative endeavor utilizes PowerShell scripting to detect failed RDP attacks by analyzing Windows Event Logs, seamlessly integrated with Azure Sentinel for real-time threat monitoring and visualization",
    "long_description": "Security Information and Event Management (SIEM) - Sentinel-Lab. This innovative endeavor utilizes PowerShell scripting to detect failed RDP attacks by analyzing Windows Event Logs, seamlessly integrated with Azure Sentinel for real-time threat monitoring and visualization.\n\nTechnologies Used\n\n• PowerShell: For scripting and automating the extraction of RDP failed logon events.\n• Microsoft Azure: Azure Sentinel is utilized as the SIEM platform.\n• ipgeolocation.io: Provides geolocation data for IP addresses.\n• GitHub: Hosting the project repository and documentation.\n• Visual Studio Code: For script development and testing.\n\nIn the provided demonstration, Azure Sentinel is configured to receive telemetry from the honeypot VM, detecting and logging failed RDP login attempts. The PowerShell script continuously monitors these logs, extracting relevant information and querying the ipgeolocation.io API to determine the geographic origin of the attackers.\n\nAttacks from Pakistan and Sri Lanka\nWorld Map of Attacks After 24 Hours",
    "skills": [
      "SIEM",
      "AZURE SENTINEL"
    ],
    "link": "https://medium.com/@lakshan.sam28/enhancing-cybersecurity-with-azure-sentinel-and-powershell-a-real-time-rdp-attack-detection-system-bdb994ba67aa",
    "categories": [
      "Defensive - Blue Teaming"
    ],
    "date": "2024-04-23",
